cells:
  - kind: 1
    value: "This notebook is for translating the columns "
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "SELECT column_name, data_type\r

      FROM user_tab_columns\r

      WHERE table_name = 'BOMEN'\r

      ORDER BY column_id;\r

      \r

      \r

      -- COLUMN_NAME DATA_TYPE    \r

      -- ----------- ------------ \r

      -- BOOMNUMMER  NUMBER       \r

      -- SOORT_NL    VARCHAR2     \r

      -- SRT_WETENS  VARCHAR2     \r

      -- LEEFTIJD    NUMBER       \r

      -- LFTDKLASSE  VARCHAR2     \r

      -- STAMDIAMET  VARCHAR2     \r

      -- EIGENAAR    VARCHAR2     \r

      -- BEHEERDER   VARCHAR2     \r

      -- SNOEIVORM   VARCHAR2     \r

      -- MONUMENTAA  VARCHAR2     \r

      -- WERKPCODE   VARCHAR2     \r

      -- WERKPAKKET  VARCHAR2     \r

      -- GROEIPLATS  VARCHAR2     \r

      -- STRAATNAAM  VARCHAR2     \r

      -- STADSDEEL   VARCHAR2     \r

      -- COUNTER     NUMBER       \r

      -- ID          NUMBER       \r

      -- WIJK        VARCHAR2     \r

      -- BUURT       VARCHAR2     \r

      -- WGS84LONG   NUMBER       \r

      -- WGS84LAT    NUMBER       \r

      -- X           NUMBER       \r

      -- Y           NUMBER       \r

      -- IEPVAK_OMS  VARCHAR2     \r

      -- PKBZ        VARCHAR2     \r

      -- GEOM        SDO_GEOMETRY \r

      \r

      \r

      Elapsed: 00:00:00.133\r

      26 rows selected."
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "\r

      ----comments\r

      \r

      COMMENT ON TABLE BOMEN IS\r

      'Individual tree records for Den Haag. Each row describes one tree and its
      point location. Dutch names and administrative labels are source data; do
      not infer botanical family from a common name.';\r

      \r

      COMMENT ON COLUMN BOMEN.BOOMNUMMER IS\r

      'Tree number recorded by the source system; do not assume it is the
      database row ID.';\r

      \r

      COMMENT ON COLUMN BOMEN.SOORT_NL IS\r

      'Dutch common name of the tree species. Translate using botanical context;
      do not translate individual words literally.';\r

      \r

      COMMENT ON COLUMN BOMEN.SRT_WETENS IS\r

      'Scientific botanical name of the tree species. Preserve the name; do not
      translate it.';\r

      \r

      COMMENT ON COLUMN BOMEN.LEEFTIJD IS\r

      'Recorded age of the tree; confirm the source unit before interpreting
      numeric values.';\r

      \r

      COMMENT ON COLUMN BOMEN.LFTDKLASSE IS\r

      'Source age-class category for the tree.';\r

      \r

      COMMENT ON COLUMN BOMEN.STAMDIAMET IS\r

      'Source trunk-diameter field; inspect values to determine whether it
      contains measurements or diameter classes.';\r

      \r

      COMMENT ON COLUMN BOMEN.EIGENAAR IS\r

      'Recorded owner of the tree. Names of people or organisations are proper
      names, not translation targets.';\r

      \r

      COMMENT ON COLUMN BOMEN.BEHEERDER IS\r

      'Recorded manager or organisation responsible for managing the tree.';\r

      \r

      COMMENT ON COLUMN BOMEN.SNOEIVORM IS\r

      'Recorded pruning form or pruning category for the tree.';\r

      \r

      COMMENT ON COLUMN BOMEN.MONUMENTAA IS\r

      'Source monumental-tree field. Its exact values and whether it represents
      status or a reference number must be verified.';\r

      \r

      COMMENT ON COLUMN BOMEN.WERKPCODE IS\r

      'Source work-package code. Preserve code values; do not translate
      them.';\r

      \r

      COMMENT ON COLUMN BOMEN.WERKPAKKET IS\r

      'Source work-package description or category associated with tree
      management.';\r

      \r

      COMMENT ON COLUMN BOMEN.GROEIPLATS IS\r

      'Source growing-site or planting-site construction category.';\r

      \r

      COMMENT ON COLUMN BOMEN.STRAATNAAM IS\r

      'Street name associated with the tree. It is a proper place name; do not
      translate it.';\r

      \r

      COMMENT ON COLUMN BOMEN.STADSDEEL IS\r

      'Recorded city district name. Preserve the place name.';\r

      \r

      COMMENT ON COLUMN BOMEN.COUNTER IS\r

      'Numeric source field named COUNTER. Its business meaning has not been
      verified; do not treat it as a tree count without checking.';\r

      \r

      COMMENT ON COLUMN BOMEN.ID IS\r

      'Source record ID used to identify a tree row. Do not assume it equals
      BOOMNUMMER.';\r

      \r

      COMMENT ON COLUMN BOMEN.WIJK IS\r

      'Recorded district or ward name. Preserve the place name.';\r

      \r

      COMMENT ON COLUMN BOMEN.BUURT IS\r

      'Recorded neighbourhood label. For geometric containment, use GEOM with a
      neighbourhood polygon rather than assuming this text is a spatial join
      key.';\r

      \r

      COMMENT ON COLUMN BOMEN.WGS84LONG IS\r

      'Tree longitude in WGS84 geographic coordinates.';\r

      \r

      COMMENT ON COLUMN BOMEN.WGS84LAT IS\r

      'Tree latitude in WGS84 geographic coordinates.';\r

      \r

      COMMENT ON COLUMN BOMEN.X IS\r

      'Source projected X coordinate. Check the coordinate reference system
      before using it for distance calculations.';\r

      \r

      COMMENT ON COLUMN BOMEN.Y IS\r

      'Source projected Y coordinate. Check the coordinate reference system
      before using it for distance calculations.';\r

      \r

      COMMENT ON COLUMN BOMEN.IEPVAK_OMS IS\r

      'Source text field IEPVAK_OMS. Its precise business definition has not
      been verified; preserve its values.';\r

      \r

      COMMENT ON COLUMN BOMEN.PKBZ IS\r

      'Source code PKBZ. Its business definition has not been verified; preserve
      its values.';\r

      \r

      COMMENT ON COLUMN BOMEN.GEOM IS\r

      'SDO_GEOMETRY point location of the individual tree. For GeoJSON maps,
      transform to SRID 4326 before calling SDO_UTIL.TO_GEOJSON.';\r

      \r

      \r

      \r\n"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "---check comments \r

      SELECT column_name, comments\r

      FROM user_col_comments\r

      WHERE table_name = 'BOMEN'\r

      ORDER BY column_name;\r

      \r

      -- COLUMN_NAME
      COMMENTS                                                                                                                                             \
      \r

      -- -----------
      -------------------------------------------------------------------------\
      -------------------------------------------------------------------------\
      -- \r

      -- BEHEERDER   Recorded manager or organisation responsible for managing
      the
      tree.                                                                                  \
      \r

      -- BOOMNUMMER  Tree number recorded by the source system; do not assume it
      is the database row
      ID.                                                                  \r

      -- BUURT       Recorded neighbourhood label. For geometric containment,
      use GEOM with a neighbourhood polygon rather than assuming this text is a
      spatial join key. "
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "--- translate procedure nl2en\r

      --- new table avaialbe \r

      \r

      CREATE OR REPLACE PROCEDURE translate_table_to_en (\r

      \    p_source_name  IN VARCHAR2,\r

      \    p_target_name  IN VARCHAR2,\r

      \    p_profile_name IN VARCHAR2\r

      ) AS\r

      \    v_source      VARCHAR2(128) := UPPER(TRIM(p_source_name));\r

      \    v_target      VARCHAR2(128) := UPPER(TRIM(p_target_name));\r

      \    v_reply       CLOB;\r

      \    v_english     VARCHAR2(128);\r

      \    v_select_list CLOB;\r

      \    v_count       NUMBER;\r

      \    v_used_names  VARCHAR2(32767) := '|';\r

      BEGIN\r

      \    -- Accept simple table names in the current schema only.\r

      \    IF NOT REGEXP_LIKE(v_source, '^[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*$')\r

      \       OR NOT REGEXP_LIKE(v_target, '^[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*$') THEN\r

      \        RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20001, 'Use simple table names in the
      current schema.');\r

      \    END IF;\r

      \r

      \    SELECT COUNT(*) INTO v_count\r

      \    FROM user_tables\r

      \    WHERE table_name = v_source;\r

      \r

      \    IF v_count = 0 THEN\r

      \        RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20002, 'Source table does not
      exist.');\r

      \    END IF;\r

      \r

      \    SELECT COUNT(*) INTO v_count\r

      \    FROM user_objects\r

      \    WHERE object_name = v_target;\r

      \r

      \    IF v_count > 0 THEN\r

      \        RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20003, 'Target name already exists;
      nothing was replaced.');\r

      \    END IF;\r

      \r

      \    FOR c IN (\r

      \        SELECT tc.column_name, tc.data_type, cc.comments\r

      \        FROM user_tab_columns tc\r

      \        LEFT JOIN user_col_comments cc\r

      \          ON cc.table_name = tc.table_name\r

      \         AND cc.column_name = tc.column_name\r

      \        WHERE tc.table_name = v_source\r

      \        ORDER BY tc.column_id\r

      \    ) LOOP\r

      \        v_reply := DBMS_CLOUD_AI.GENERATE(\r

      \            prompt =>\r

      \                'Translate this database column name into clear English.
      ' ||\r

      \                'Return ONLY one uppercase SQL identifier using letters,
      digits, ' ||\r

      \                'and underscores; no explanation or punctuation. ' ||\r

      \                'Preserve its meaning and do not invent a meaning for an
      unknown code. ' ||\r

      \                'Table: ' || v_source ||\r

      \                '. Column: ' || c.column_name ||\r

      \                '. Data type: ' || c.data_type ||\r

      \                '. Description: ' || NVL(c.comments, 'Not available.'),\r

      \            profile_name => p_profile_name,\r

      \            action       => 'chat'\r

      \        );\r

      \r

      \        v_english := UPPER(TRIM(DBMS_LOB.SUBSTR(v_reply, 128, 1)));\r

      \r

      \        IF NOT REGEXP_LIKE(v_english, '^[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*$') THEN\r

      \            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(\r

      \                -20004, 'Invalid English name for ' || c.column_name\r

      \            );\r

      \        END IF;\r

      \r

      \        IF INSTR(v_used_names, '|' || v_english || '|') > 0 THEN\r

      \            RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(\r

      \                -20005, 'Duplicate English name: ' || v_english\r

      \            );\r

      \        END IF;\r

      \r

      \        v_used_names := v_used_names || v_english || '|';\r

      \r

      \        IF v_select_list IS NOT NULL THEN\r

      \            v_select_list := v_select_list || ', ';\r

      \        END IF;\r

      \r

      \        v_select_list := v_select_list ||\r

      \            '\"' || REPLACE(c.column_name, '\"', '\"\"') ||\r

      \            '\" AS \"' || v_english || '\"';\r

      \    END LOOP;\r

      \r

      \    EXECUTE IMMEDIATE\r

      \        'CREATE TABLE \"' || v_target || '\" AS SELECT ' ||\r

      \        v_select_list || ' FROM \"' || v_source || '\"';\r

      END;\r

      /\r\n"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "\r

      -- run to translate your columns\r

      \r

      BEGIN\r

      \    translate_table_to_en(\r

      \        p_source_name  => 'BOMEN',\r

      \        p_target_name  => 'BOMEN_TREES',\r

      \        p_profile_name => 'OCI_GROK_4_3_BOMEN_BURRT_PROFILE'\r

      \    );\r

      END;\r

      /"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "SELECT column_id, column_name, data_type\r

      FROM user_tab_columns\r

      WHERE table_name = 'BOMEN_TREES'\r

      ORDER BY column_id;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "desc BOMEN_TREES\r

